      "side": 1,
      "message": "Thanks, that makes sense to ask. The bug is a correctness issue for square row-major matrices, not a performance optimization. The previous lowering mostly discovered work by seeing that the matrix type changed after row-major rewriting. For square matrices, the logical type remains `matNxN`, so after the struct member\u0027s row-major decoration is removed, later uses can look type-identical and skip the required semantic transpose.\n\nThe updated patch tracks pointer provenance for values that still refer to physical row-major storage. Changing the ordinary matrix type would not really solve the square case unless we introduced some separate transient row-major matrix marker/type through the IR, which seemed like a larger design change for this fix.",
      "parentUuid": "08865cc6_6fa0369b",
      "revId": "4980e21bb32ae66e5b91e95117b467fa065eb411",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
