      "side": 1,
      "message": "The source can now be either an `Access` or a `Let` that aliases a row-major matrix pointer. That happens when we split an aliased matrix-vector access and use a `let` to carry the matrix pointer plus the saved column index. Keeping this as the more general instruction result lets both direct accesses and let aliases flow through the same load/store-vector-element path.",
      "parentUuid": "5a2b021b_58eb58c0",
