      "writtenOn": "2026-06-02T09:38:48Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This can happen for a single-index access through an alias to the matrix pointer, for example `let m \u003d \u0026(s.m); m[i]`. When we pop the final index to save it as the row/column index, there are no indices left for the `Access` instruction. Since `Access` needs at least one index, the patch creates a `let` for the matrix pointer and records the popped index alongside it.",
      "parentUuid": "5b226bb5_bff36cfb",
